<configtype typenbr = "1">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1416014" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Check Valve Inspection
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1416013">Check Valve Removal and Installation:K14C</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Check check valve as follows.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If check result is not as specified, replace check valve.
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
If excessive negative pressure is applied, the check valve may be damaged.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Do not exceed a negative pressure of –60 kPa (–0.6 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, –8.7 psi, –0.6 bar).
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect special tool to orange side (1) of check valve and set the tool in “VACUUM” mode, check that negative pressure –60 kPa (–0.6 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, –8.7 psi, –0.6 bar) can be applied.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Before using special tool (vacuum pump gauge), read its Operator’s Manual to know how to use it.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1D112">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09917-47020">
09917–47020
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect special tool to black side (2) of check valve and check negative pressure cannot be applied.
</ptxt>
